//==
// # 09-tooling: specifications
//
// The invented constructs of SPEC-DSL.md section 3 for layer 9: the
// contracts of the host shims, the bodiless functions marked "// host:" in
// the library files. A host shim is not a deferred algorithm: its body is C#
// in the test host (README.md beside this file, "Host shims"), because it
// reads or writes a file, and Plato functions are pure. Every shim is a
// thin wrapper: the conversion to what is written is a Plato function with
// a body, so the shim only moves bytes. Read, not parsed: the gate skips
// this file.
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - Contracts: reading

//==
// # Contracts: reading

// The C# decoder of TKT-312 on one corpus file. The file is
// <root>/<entry.Source>/<entry.Name>, the collection's folder and the
// file's name within it (07-validation/README.md, "Corpus"). The result is
// what DecodeRaw gives, so it obeys layer 3's raw laws. A file that cannot
// be opened or parsed gives a RawDecodedModel whose model has no rows, unit
// Millimetre, and whose Diagnostics hold one Error with code
// "TOOLING-FILE-UNREADABLE" at Provenance.WholeInput; the shim never throws
// (layer 0's rule: diagnostics, never exceptions).
spec LoadCorpusModel(root: String, entry: CorpusEntry): RawDecodedModel
{
    ensures Law_RawHasNoClosures(result);
    ensures Law_RawTolerancesUnset(result);
    ensures Law_UnitsFactorsAgree(result);
    ensures result.Model.Unit == LengthUnit.Millimetre;
}
